Robot Intakes

Roller intake:
Uses spinning wheels/rollers.
Simple and fast.
Can slip or jam if designed poorly.

Compliant wheel intake:
Uses flexible wheels that grip the game piece.
Good for handling pieces that aren't perfectly aligned.
Needs the correct amount of compression.

Pivoting intake:
Intake moves up/down or rotates.
Can make the robot more compact.
More moving parts means more things that can break.

Compression = how much the intake presses against the game piece.

Too little → piece slips.
Too much → jams, slows the motor, or makes the motor work harder.
Goal → enough compression for a reliable grip.

